      "fallbackReason": null,
      "text": "Republicans have started openly criticizing Trump over the Iran war\n\nThere is growing discontent in the Republican Party over Donald Trump's actions in the background of the conflict with Iran. The president's associates were ready to give him time, but with one condition: the conflict should be quickly finished. Now this irritation has become public.\n\nThis week, the House of Representatives passed a resolution on military powers for the first time, which should have stopped the war with Iran. There are almost no practical consequences, but it is a political signal: four Republicans voted with the Democrats. For a party that usually follows Trump almost unanimously, this is a rare case of open dissent.\n\nRepublicans are particularly concerned about the political consequences of the conflict ahead of the congressional elections: rising oil and gasoline prices could hit ordinary Americans.\n\nTrump himself still wants a deal with Tehran and does not seek a major war. But the longer the attacks go on in the Middle East, the more pressure there will be on the White House. The main question, according to Burns, is no longer whether Trump wants an agreement, but what he will do if he doesn't get one. \n\n#Trump #GOP #War\n\n👂 More on Trump's Ear⚠️",
